# 22. NON-NEGOTIABLE REQUIREMENTS

These rules must be followed throughout development.

1. The selected PMX/PMD model is the actual target of all pose calculations.

2. Never rely exclusively on generic humanoid bone names.

3. Never blindly transfer 2D pixel coordinates into bone rotations.

4. Always account for local bone axes, hierarchy, rest pose, and model-specific IK.

5. Never introduce random rotations to missing bones.

6. Never reverse left and right limbs.

7. Never apply the same rotation twice through direct transforms and IK.

8. Never modify the source model without permission.

9. Never export fake or incomplete VPD/VMD files.

10. Keep body pose and facial morph export compatible with the actual MMD file formats.

11. Provide manual correction tools when AI confidence is insufficient.

12. Make every exported pose reusable in actual MikuMikuDance.

13. Do not claim perfect reconstruction when the reference image does not contain enough information to determine hidden 3D geometry.

14. Do not build a UI-only demonstration. Every visible control must perform its advertised function.

15. Prioritize pose accuracy, model compatibility, and data integrity over decorative features.

